The client libraries in this directory are licensed under the Apache License,
Version 2.0, separately from the server in the repository root.

That separation is deliberate. Integrating with ComplyLayer means importing a
client library into a regulated company's payment path, and a permissive licence
on that library means the integration decision never has to reach their legal
team. The server carries the Business Source License; the code you compile into
your own application does not.

